<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/condo-building.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/condo-building-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/condo-building.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/policy-and-claim-guides/">Claim guides</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Virginia FAIR Plan Claims: What VPIA Policyholders Should Know</span></nav><p class="kicker">Guide · 5 min read</p><h1>Virginia FAIR Plan Claims: What VPIA Policyholders Should Know</h1><p class="lede">What VPIA coverage typically includes, where claim disputes arise and how appraisal may help.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><p class="byline">By the Virginia Insurance Appraiser team · <time datetime="2026-08-25">August 25, 2026</time> · 5 min read</p>
<p>The Virginia Property Insurance Association (VPIA) is Virginia’s FAIR Plan. It exists to provide basic property coverage to owners who can’t find it in the regular market, often because of a property’s age, condition, location or claims history. VPIA policies can look different from a typical homeowners policy, and that affects Virginia FAIR Plan claims.</p>
<h2>What VPIA coverage often looks like</h2>
<p>FAIR Plan coverage is often more basic than a standard homeowners policy. Depending on the form you bought, it may cover fewer perils, pay actual cash value instead of replacement cost, or leave out coverages like personal liability. Read your declarations and policy form carefully, because the details vary.</p>
<h2>Where disputes arise</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>ACV settlements</strong> where depreciation takes a large share of an older home’s claim.</li>
<li><strong>Named-peril coverage</strong> where the cause of loss decides whether anything is paid.</li>
<li><strong>Older homes</strong> with plaster, slate or heart pine priced as modern materials.</li>
<li><strong>Scope disputes</strong> on storm and fire losses, as with any insurer.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Can appraisal help?</h2>
<p>If your VPIA policy contains an appraisal condition and the dispute is about the amount of loss, appraisal may be available. Check your form for the clause and its deadlines. The same limits apply: appraisal won’t decide whether a peril is covered.</p>
<h2>Depreciation on an ACV policy</h2>
<p>On an actual cash value policy, depreciation isn’t held back to be paid later. It’s permanently subtracted. That makes how depreciation is calculated especially important. The <a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/holdback-recovery-calculator/">holdback recovery calculator</a> includes an ACV-only option.</p>
<h2>Questions about VPIA itself</h2>
<p>Complaints about how a FAIR Plan claim was handled can be raised with the Bureau of Insurance, which oversees insurance in Virginia.</p>
